Z||000000||maryjane||05-30-2001||12:37 AM||||I was doing a web search on Iron Duke and came accross a Jeep site that mentioned that"a lot of people think the 2.5 4cyl in the 84 jeep Cherokee is the Gm iron Duke but is actually a Pontiac engine designed to replace the GM Duke." or at least words to that effect. Is this eng related to the Duke in the 84 Fiero? founf it at<BR> offroad.com/jeep/tech/engine/amc150.html<BR>Sorry, couldn't make it a link<BR>Don & Jane<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||MrPBody||05-30-2001||09:47 AM||||This is all hearsay, so not worth crap in a court of law:<P>In the early 80's, Jeep used the Iron Duke and the GM V-6 in Cherokees.  Later (1987?), they switched to a 4.0-liter inline 6-cylinder and a Jeep 2.5-liter 4-cylinder.<P>A few past posts have speculated whether the Jeep 2.5 could be swapped into a Fiero, but the consensus is "Why bother?"<BR>||||reg||1
